iris-desktop-skin (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Skin rewrite against upstream sources; removal of the destructive config
    set that a previous revision shipped.
  * theme/Iris/cinnamon/cinnamon.css: rebuilt using only selector names that
    Cinnamon actually defines (the previous file styled 6 non-existent
    classes, so the panel rules were inert) and St-correct properties:
    background-blur, border-radius-topleft (not border-top-left-radius).
  * theme/Iris/gtk-3.0/gtk.css: SSD window frames now styled through the nodes
    Muffin really reads (window.ssd > decoration > headerbar), including the
    titlebar border-radius Muffin uses to clip corners.
  * theme/Iris/metacity-1/metacity-theme-3.xml: REMOVED. Muffin has no
    metacity XML parser, so the file could never have had any effect.
  * dconf/iris-settings: REMOVED, replaced by
    config/gsettings/iris.gsettings and scripts/apply-settings.sh, which
    validates every schema/key against the installed schemas and backs up the
    previous values. The old file wrote keys that do not exist (org.cinnamon
    theme, panel-positions, panel-heights, desktop.interface
    color-scheme/document-font-name, background show-desktop-icons,
    notifications icon-size) and used two applet UUIDs that are not Cinnamon
    applets.
  * scripts/install.sh: no longer overwrites /etc/lightdm/lightdm.conf, no
    longer installs a plymouth theme, no longer runs apt or writes dconf by
    default, and refuses to replace a desktop while a graphical session is
    live. Manifest plus ownership marker so uninstall is exact instead of
    `rm -rf`.
  * config/package-lists/iris-core.list.chroot: dropped the non-existent
    plymouth-theme-iris / nm-applet / gpaste entries (they failed
    `lb build`) and added the required xwayland dependency for the Wayland
    session.
  * tools/check-theme.py and CI: static gate for the whole class of problems
    above, plus an install/uninstall round-trip job on debian:trixie.
  * Packaging: debhelper auto* overrides (there is nothing to compile, and the
    root Makefile must not be mistaken for a build system), dh_missing set to
    list rather than fail, session entries still registered, QA tooling left
    out of the binary package so a data package does not pull in python3.

